    "body": "Depends on: nothing (can start anytime; consumes #59 pipeline). The confirmed D3 distribution includes a Simple English Wikipedia natural partition (CC BY-SA 4.0, SPDX in PROV) that does not exist as data yet. Produce it: fetch a pinned Simple Wiki snapshot, shard-generate teacher observations via the observe CLI into .uor-models, write the corpus manifest with CID + license, and record the held-out split rule. Acceptance: manifest committed under .uor-models with CID; the first full Gate C run on the natural partition prints in the issue; PROV section of produced artifacts references the corpus CID.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- A pinned Simple English Wikipedia corpus exists as teacher observations under `.uor-models/`, with a manifest carrying its CID and SPDX `CC-BY-SA-4.0` license.\n- The held-out split rule is fixed in the manifest and the first full Gate C run on the natural partition is posted here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Manifest committed with corpus CID, license identifier, article count, and split rule.\n- [ ] Observations are generated via the observe pipeline (content-addressed sample IDs, resumable shards).\n- [ ] PROV sections of artifacts built on it reference the corpus CID.\n- [ ] The natural-partition Gate C 4-way table is in this thread.",
